infographic sequence-ascending-steps
data
  title 0-RTT replay defense — three layers, all required
  desc The ciphertext is replayable, so safety comes from layered policy, not the TLS layer. Skip one and a single non-idempotent POST double-executes.
  order asc
  sequences
    - label 1. Restrict 0-RTT to idempotent requests
      desc GET, HEAD and safe operations only — replaying them is a no-op. POST, DELETE and state-changing requests wait for 1-RTT keys. Stops unsafe requests entering 0-RTT at all.
    - label 2. 425 Too Early escape hatch
      desc Proxy forwards 0-RTT with Early-Data: 1; the origin replies 425 (RFC 8470), forcing a retry after the full handshake. Catches anything that slips past layer 1.
    - label 3. Isolate session ticket keys per server
      desc No shared ticket keys across data centers; 1-24 h lifetimes. A ticket from Server A is valid only on Server A — limits the blast radius of a captured packet.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b #f43f5e
